{
  "uid": "chiya-traces",
  "title": "Day 3 - Traces and correlation",
  "description": "Metrics find it, logs identify it, traces explain it. The trace_id field is the join.",
  "tags": [
    "chiya",
    "day3",
    "traces"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "refresh": "10s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-30m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to use this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### The three-pillar workflow\n\n1. **Metrics** (top row) tell you *something is slow* and how slow.\n2. **Logs** (bottom) tell you *which requests* were slow.\n3. Expand any log line and click **TraceID → View trace in Jaeger**. That tells you *where the time went*.\n\nStep 3 works because `app/src/logger.ts` writes `trace_id` onto every request-scoped log line, and\n`grafana/provisioning/datasources/datasources.yml` defines a derived field that turns it into a link.\nTwo systems that have never heard of each other, joined by one shared id.\n\nJaeger UI directly: [http://localhost:16686](http://localhost:16686)"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "1. Metrics: something is slow",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "title": "p95 — /teas/:id/pairings",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "description": "Yesterday this number was the end of the road. Today it is the start.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(chiya_http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{route=\"/teas/:id/pairings\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "decimals": 3,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.2
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.5
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "title": "p95 latency by route",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 9,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 7
      },
      "description": "One route is obviously the problem. Notice what this cannot tell you: WHY. Same data as Day 2, same dead end.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, route) (rate(chiya_http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "range": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{route}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            },
            "showPoints": "never",
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "title": "Event loop lag (p99) — the blocking evidence",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 9,
        "x": 15,
        "y": 7
      },
      "description": "The pairings endpoint has a 120ms span that WAITS on a fake supplier API and a ~75ms span that BLOCKS the CPU. Only the blocking one shows up here. Raise BLEND_ITERATIONS and watch this climb; raise the supplier sleep and it will not move.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "nodejs_eventloop_lag_p99_seconds",
          "range": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 25,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            },
            "showPoints": "never",
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "2. Logs: which requests — expand a line, click TraceID",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "logs",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "title": "Slow requests (over 200ms)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      },
      "description": "The JSON is parsed at query time, then filtered numerically on durationMs. Expand a line and look for the TraceID link.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "{service=\"api\"} | json | durationMs > 200",
          "queryType": "range"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "showLabels": false,
        "showCommonLabels": false,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "prettifyLogMessage": true,
        "enableLogDetails": true,
        "dedupStrategy": "none",
        "sortOrder": "Descending"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "logs",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "title": "Errors",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 14
      },
      "description": "Every one of these carries a trace_id, so every failure is one click from a trace showing exactly where it died.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "{service=\"api\", level=\"error\"}",
          "queryType": "range"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "showLabels": false,
        "showCommonLabels": false,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "prettifyLogMessage": true,
        "enableLogDetails": true,
        "dedupStrategy": "none",
        "sortOrder": "Descending"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "3. Context: is this affecting everyone?",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 25
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "title": "Requests / sec by route",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 26
      },
      "description": "The slow endpoint is only ~4% of traffic. Blocking the event loop means it damages the other 96% too.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (route) (rate(chiya_http_requests_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "range": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{route}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
